- Three sources of one node: its `view.tree` declaration, its method and its rule.
- Port of the source panel of studio, down to the deck of three code editors.
-
- A node is a flat property of the class after normalization, so the three texts of
- a node are three slices of the three texts of the class: the declaration, the
- method of that name in the body, and the rule addressed to the attribute the
- framework writes on it. The whole class is one switch away, and that switch is
- the whole difference between the two modes.
- @see ../../ARCHITECTURE.md sections 1 and 2
$bog_vmap_app_code $mol_view
	- The root class of the document.
	klass \
	- Property name of the picked node, empty when nothing is picked. Without one
	- there is nothing to slice and the panel edits the class whole.
	prop \
	- Methods this node needs written by hand: the names its declaration refers to
	- that the class does not generate. The JS tab edits exactly these, because a
	- method named after the node itself would shadow the factory of the sub-view
	- and take the node off the canvas.
	hooks /string
	source? \
	- The same value the inspector edits, so a change made with the mouse shows up
	- in the text without a path of its own.
	node_source? \
	js? \
	css? \
	- What the scene said about this node last, empty when it said nothing.
	error \
	whole? false
	- Why the last edit was not written into the document, empty when it was.
	refusal? \
	sub <= content /$mol_view
	Head $mol_bar
		sub <= head_content /$mol_view
	Scope_note $mol_view
		sub / <= scope_note \
	Scope $mol_check
		title \Весь класс
		hint \Править класс целиком, а не выбранный узел. Какой это класс, сказано в шапке: у узла со своим классом — его, у остальных — тот, который узел объявляет
		checked? <=> whole?
	- Here and not only in the status strip: an error belongs where the code that
	- caused it is being written.
	Alarm $mol_view
		sub / <= error
	- The refused text stays in the field so it can be fixed; the document keeps the
	- last one that parsed.
	Refusal $mol_view
		sub / <= note \
	- Parameters without types in the body of this node. Shown while it is being
	- written, because the failure they cause happens at the export, where neither
	- the mistake nor its author is any more.
	Typing $mol_view
		sub <= typing_rows /$mol_view
	Typing_row* $mol_view
		sub / <= typing_text* \
	Sources $mol_deck
		items <= source_tabs /$mol_view
	Tree $mol_textarea
		title \view.tree
		hint \Имя_узла $mol_view
		sidebar_showed true
		value? <=> tree_text? \
	Js $mol_textarea
		title \JS
		hint \
		sidebar_showed true
		value? <=> js_text? \
	- What stands on the JS tab when this node has no method of its own to write.
	- A state, not an empty field: an empty field here would invite writing a method
	- named after the node, and that one shadows the factory of the sub-view.
	Js_idle $mol_view
		title \JS
		sub / <= js_idle_note \
	Css $mol_textarea
		title \CSS
		hint \
		sidebar_showed true
		value? <=> css_text? \
